{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he spoke to their heart.</b> Words that find acceptance in the heart — 'Before you came down here, people were murmuring about me that I am a slave; through you it became known that I am a free man. And if I kill you, what will people say? A group of young men he saw and praised, and said, \"They are my brothers\" — and in the end he killed them. Do you have a brother who kills his brothers?' Another interpretation: 'Ten lamps could not extinguish one lamp,' and so forth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:29.159795349Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}